cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the released result files, please cite both the
  accompanying paper and the KurdiSent corpus it is built on.
title: >-
  kusa - Morphology-Aware Sentiment Analysis for Sorani Kurdish
abstract: >-
  Code and reproducibility artefacts for a dual-view adaptation of the SARF
  architecture to Sorani Kurdish sentiment analysis on the KurdiSent corpus,
  evaluated under a leakage-controlled held-out protocol with a capacity-matched
  control that separates the architectural gain from the morphological one.
  Also releases the blind re-annotation audit of the corpus labels as a
  text-free per-item table, which can be rejoined against KurdiSent on the item
  identifier. The KurdiSent corpus itself is not redistributed here.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/lawanmai/Kusa'
keywords:
  - sentiment analysis
  - Sorani Kurdish
  - low-resource NLP
  - morphology
  - multi-view learning
  - XLM-RoBERTa
  - reproducibility
  - annotation quality
  - inter-annotator agreement
  - less-resourced languages
